// Seven equal bars on a 3:5 field.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Bigender pride flag"
  designer "no-bucks-for-this-doe (Tumblr)"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  render-license "CC0-1.0"
  date "2014-07"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20220531074105/https://pridearchive.tumblr.com/post/93315678776/bigender-pride"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20250124113555/https://nonbinary.wiki/wiki/Bigender"
  source "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bigender_Flag.svg"
  note "The Pride Archive post of 30 July 2014 credits the flag to Tumblr user no-bucks-for-this-doe and gives two versions, the middle stripe plain white or white fading to gray. This file is the plain-white one. Pinks mean femininity, blues masculinity, purple nonbinary, white agender and neutral genders. The date is that of the earliest source I read, not necessarily the designer's own first post."
  note "The post's image (a 492 by 296 JPEG, read) has seven equal stripes. The post gives no hex or proportion. The colors are the Commons drawing's; the post's image samples within JPEG error of them (#c479a0, #eca6cb, #d5c7e8, #ffffff, #9ac7e8, #6c83cf). The 3:5 proportion is the common format, near the image's 1.66."
}
palette {
  pink "#c479a2"
  light-pink "#eda5cd"
  lavender "#d5c7e8"
  white "#ffffff"
  light-blue "#9ac7e8"
  blue "#6d82d1"
}
proportion hoist=3 fly=5

bars pink light-pink lavender white lavender light-blue blue
